# Next.js on Cloudflare — CVFairy Project Rules

## Stack Overview

| Layer | Technology | Notes |
|-------|-----------|-------|
| Framework | Next.js 16 (App Router) | TypeScript strict mode |
| Deployment | Cloudflare Workers via **vinext** (preferred) or **@opennextjs/cloudflare** (stable fallback) | NOT `@cloudflare/next-on-pages` — archived Sept 2025 |
| Database | Cloudflare D1 (SQLite) | Via binding `env.DB` |
| ORM | Drizzle ORM (`drizzle-orm/d1`) | Drizzle Kit with `d1-http` driver for migrations |
| Object Storage | Cloudflare R2 | Via binding `env.R2` — zero egress fees |
| KV Cache | Cloudflare Workers KV | Via binding `env.KV` |
| AI | Cloudflare Workers AI | Via binding `env.AI` |
| CSS | Tailwind CSS v4 | |
| Testing | Vitest + Miniflare | Workers-native test environment |
| Config | `wrangler.jsonc` | Preferred over `wrangler.toml` for new projects |

## Deployment Path Decision

### vinext (Recommended for new projects)
Cloudflare's Vite-based reimplementation of the Next.js API surface. Faster builds, smaller bundles, native Workers integration.

```bash
npx vinext init --platform=cloudflare   # migrate existing project
npx @vinext/cloudflare deploy           # build + deploy in one command
```

### @opennextjs/cloudflare (Stable fallback)
Use when vinext has a compatibility gap with a specific Next.js feature you need.

```bash
npx @opennextjs/cloudflare build        # build
npx wrangler deploy                      # deploy
```

### NEVER use `@cloudflare/next-on-pages`
Archived September 2025. Does not support Next.js 15+, ISR, or modern features.

