## Cloudflare Free Tier Limits (enforce these constraints)

All daily limits reset at 00:00 UTC.

| Service | Free Tier Limit | Key Constraint |
|---------|----------------|----------------|
| **Workers** | 100K requests/day, 10ms CPU/request | 3 MiB compressed bundle, 50 subrequests/invocation |
| **D1** | 5M rows read/day, 100K rows written/day | 5 GB total storage |
| **R2** | 10 GB storage, 1M Class A ops/mo, 10M Class B ops/mo | Zero egress fees |
| **KV** | 100K reads/day, 1K writes/day | 1 GB storage |
| **Workers AI** | 10K neurons/day | Shared across all models; large models burn faster |
| **Pages** | 500 builds/month | 20K static asset files |
| **Worker size** | 3 MiB (free), 10 MiB (paid) | After gzip compression |

### Staying Within Free Tier

- Use `force-static` or `force-dynamic` explicitly on every route — never let Next.js guess.
- Prefer R2 over KV for storing anything larger than 25 KB (KV value limit is 25 MiB but writes are expensive at 1K/day).
- Use D1 `batch()` for atomic multi-statement operations — one batch = one write toward the daily limit.
- Cache aggressively with `Cache-Control` headers to reduce Worker invocations.
- For Workers AI: prefer small models (Llama 3.2 1B ≈ 5.6 neurons/request) over large ones (Llama 3.1 70B ≈ 62 neurons/request).
- Monitor usage via Cloudflare Dashboard > Workers & Pages > Metrics.

