## R2 Object Storage Patterns

```typescript
// Upload
async function uploadFile(env: CloudflareEnv, key: string, body: ReadableStream, contentType: string) {
  await env.R2.put(key, body, {
    httpMetadata: { contentType },
  });
}

// Download
async function getFile(env: CloudflareEnv, key: string) {
  const object = await env.R2.get(key);
  if (!object) return new Response("Not found", { status: 404 });
  return new Response(object.body, {
    headers: {
      "Content-Type": object.httpMetadata?.contentType ?? "application/octet-stream",
      "Cache-Control": "public, max-age=86400",
    },
  });
}

// Delete
async function deleteFile(env: CloudflareEnv, key: string) {
  await env.R2.delete(key);
}

// List with prefix
const listed = await env.R2.list({ prefix: `users/${userId}/` });
```

### R2 Rules
- Use structured key prefixes: `users/{userId}/resumes/{filename}`
- Set `Cache-Control` headers for browser caching.
- Prefer R2 over KV for files > 25 KB.
- R2 Class A ops (PUT, DELETE, LIST) cost more — minimize list operations.
- Maximum object size: 5 TB. Maximum key length: 1024 bytes.

