## Workers AI Patterns

```typescript
export async function POST(request: Request) {
  const { env } = await getCloudflareContext();
  const { prompt } = await request.json();

  const response = await env.AI.run("@cf/meta/llama-3.2-1b-instruct", {
    messages: [
      { role: "system", content: "You are a helpful career advisor." },
      { role: "user", content: prompt },
    ],
    max_tokens: 512,
  });

  return Response.json(response);
}
```

### Workers AI Rules
- 10K neurons/day shared across ALL models. Budget per feature.
- Small models (~5 neurons/request) vs large models (~60 neurons/request) — pick intentionally.
- Handle error code 3036 (HTTP 429) = daily neuron limit exceeded. Show graceful fallback.
- Use streaming responses for better UX: `stream: true` option.
- Text embeddings cost ~1-5 neurons/request — efficient for search.
- Image generation costs ~300-500 neurons/call — extremely expensive on free tier.

